==English==

===Etymology===
From English [[colre]], from Old French colre, from Latin [[cholera]], "[[jaundice]]", from {{etyl|grc}} [[kholera]], from [[khol]], "[[bile]]"

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkɑlɝɪk/|/kəˈlɛɹɪk/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Easily becoming [[angry]].
# Showing or expressing [[anger]].

====Synonyms====
* [[wrathful]], [[irate]], [[angry]], [[indignant]], [[vexed]]

